Third-party code
----------------
elimgui is a reimplementation of Dear ImGui (https://github.com/ocornut/imgui),
Copyright (c) 2014-2026 Omar Cornut, MIT License. It follows Dear ImGui's API
and behaviour, and in places its exact values: the built-in color themes
(include/eli/style/eli_style_colors.h), the default style sizes
(include/eli/core/eli_context.h), the CRC32 ID-hash and storage semantics
(include/eli/id/), and the RGB/HSV conversion ported in
include/eli/style/eli_style_color_utils.h.

vendor/stb/stb_truetype.h (v1.26) and vendor/stb/stb_rect_pack.h (v1.01) are
from stb (https://github.com/nothings/stb), Copyright (c) 2017 Sean Barrett,
available under the MIT License or as public domain (Unlicense); elimgui uses
them under the MIT License. Each file carries its license text at its end.

include/eli/font/eli_font_proggy.h embeds ProggyClean.ttf,
Copyright (c) 2004, 2005 Tristan Grimmer, MIT License, in stb's compressed
form. Its decompressor is a port of stb_decompress from stb (Sean Barrett),
public domain.

vendor/jaclibc is a git submodule (not part of this tree) holding JACLibc
(https://github.com/dcherrera/jaclibc), Copyright (c) 2025 FRINKnet and
Friends, MIT License. WebAssembly builds link it; native builds use the
system libc.

The MIT License text is in LICENSES/MIT.txt.


